[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/issues/comments/5751322743","html_url":"https://github.com/Agent-Field/CodeAF/issues/1297#issuecomment-5751322743","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/issues/1297","id":5751322743,"node_id":"IC_kwDOTu5AHM8AAAABVs44dw","user":{"login":"santoshkumarradha","id":29346072,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5MzQ2MDcy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29346072?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha","html_url":"https://github.com/santoshkumarradha","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-20T17:11:05Z","updated_at":"2026-09-20T17:11:05Z","body":"A second failure mode, found the same evening, and it is the one worth designing against.\n\nThe lock is advisory, so the natural way to misuse it is not to ignore it. It is to POLL IT AND THEN NOT TAKE IT. Two independent tools were found doing exactly that, written by different people who had both clearly read the lock and meant to respect it:\n\n- one waits for the lock to read free, then runs whole-package tests outside it, 23 times in series;\n- another runs a full package suite directly with no wrapper at all.\n\nThe first is the interesting one. Waiting for free and then proceeding without holding is a reasonable-looking reading of an advisory lock, and it produces the worst outcome available: the tool believes it is being polite, every other reader sees the file free, and the box carries a full suite that nothing accounts for. The author of the first found it in their own tooling after seeing the second, and has since made it hold the lock for the whole pass.\n\nSo the lock currently answers \"is anyone holding this\" and is routinely asked as if it answered \"is the box free\". The gap between those two questions cost several hours in one session: a gate went red on a test whose own comment says it reproduces a loaded box, and three separate readers each concluded the machine was quiet when it was not.\n\nWorth deciding alongside the orphan question:\n\n- whether the helper should make holding the easy path and polling the hard one, rather than the reverse;\n- whether anything should be able to see that a heavy suite is running without having to take the lock to find out;\n- whether a suite started outside the lock can be made to fail loudly rather than silently succeed.\n\nFiled as observation, not as a proposed fix.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/issues/comments/5751322743/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"santoshkumarradha","id":29346072,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5MzQ2MDcy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29346072?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha","html_url":"https://github.com/santoshkumarradha","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha/gists